{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PoincareLefschetzBorromean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PoincareLefschetzBorromean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BorromeanVolumeCatalan"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.not_poincareLefschetz_of_h1_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.not_poincareLefschetz_of_h1_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L178-L189","doc":"The fields **discriminate**: a datum with `b₁ = 2` is not a Poincaré–Lefschetz\nBorromean datum.\n\nWithout this, \"the class is satisfiable\" is compatible with the class being\nsatisfied by everything, which is the failure mode the empty carrier had. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanHomologyModel_satisfies","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanHomologyModel_satisfies","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L166-L176","doc":"The three fields are jointly satisfiable.\n\nA `theorem`, deliberately **not** an `instance`: as an instance it would be found\nby resolution only for this datum, but making it one invites the next reader to add\n`instance` to a datum that is *not* constructed to satisfy the fields. Cf. the\n`trivialSkeinGenerationContext` note in `QOU/Torsion/skein_generation.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanHomologyModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromeanHomologyModel","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L156-L164","doc":"A datum satisfying all three fields, so the class is not an empty carrier.\n\nConstructed to satisfy them — `rankHrel` is *defined* as the dual of `rankH`, and\n`plPairing` is *defined* as `vol_B3`. It therefore shows consistency and nothing\nmore; it is not a model of the Borromean complement and asserts nothing about it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bettiB3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bettiB3","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L148-L154","doc":"Betti numbers of a 3-component link complement in `S³`:\n`b₀ = 1`, `b₁ = 3`, `b₂ = 2`, `b_k = 0` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plPairing_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plPairing_pos","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L139-L146","doc":"The pairing is strictly positive — a real consequence, not a restatement:\nit follows from the conjectural field together with a *proved* fact about\nCatalan's constant, and would fail for a datum whose pairing were `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plPairing_eq_eight_catalan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.plPairing_eq_eight_catalan","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L133-L137","doc":"The pairing is `8G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rankHrel_two_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.rankHrel_two_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L121-L131","doc":"The block's \"in particular\": `H²(M, ∂M)` has rank 3, matching `H₁`.\n\n**Derived**, and this is the point of the re-encoding — it is none of the three\nfields, and it needs two of them. The previous carrier could not state it, because\nit stated nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.pairing_eq_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.pairing_eq_vol","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The top Poincaré–Lefschetz pairing is the hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.h1_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.h1_rank","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L117-L117","doc":"`H₁ ≅ ℤ³` — three meridian classes, one per Borromean component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.duality","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Poincaré–Lefschetz duality, at the level of ranks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PoincareLefschetzBorromean","kind":"class","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L96-L119","doc":"**Poincaré–Lefschetz closure on the Borromean complement.**\n\nTwo classical hypotheses and one framework claim, over an abstract datum `D`.\n\n* `duality` — Poincaré–Lefschetz: `rank H^k(M, ∂M) = rank H_{3-k}(M)` in degrees\n  `k ≤ 3`. Classical; cited, not conjectured.\n* `h1_rank` — `H₁(S³ ∖ 𝓑₃) ≅ ℤ³`, the three meridian classes. Standard for a\n  3-component link complement; cited, not conjectured.\n* `pairing_eq_vol` — **this is the conjecture**: the top pairing is the hyperbolic\n  volume `Vol(𝓑₃) = 8G`.\n\n`D` is a parameter, so a `[PoincareLefschetzBorromean D]` binder is a hypothesis\nabout the caller's datum rather than about one the instance chose. No instance is\nsupplied for any datum other than the consistency witness below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:poincare-lefschetz-borromean","label":"conj:poincare-lefschetz-borromean","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.plPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.plPairing","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L94-L94","doc":"the top-degree Poincaré–Lefschetz pairing `⟨vol, [M]⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.rankHrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.rankHrel","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L92-L92","doc":"rank of `H^k(M, ∂M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.rankH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.rankH","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L90-L90","doc":"rank of `H_k(M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanHomology","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/poincare-lefschetz-borromean.lean#L78-L94","doc":"The homological data of a cusped 3-manifold that the block consumes.\n\n`rankH k` is the rank of `H_k(M)`, `rankHrel k` the rank of `H^k(M, ∂M)`, and\n`plPairing` the value of the top-degree Poincaré–Lefschetz pairing of the volume\nform against the fundamental class.\n\nRanks rather than groups: the block's use of the duality is the rank statement\n(\"in particular `H²(∂𝓑₃) ≅ H₁ ≅ ℤ³`\"), and recording groups would require the\nmanifold-with-cusps machinery the block itself lists as missing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}